[{"id":3182844396,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc69tlns","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally on Fedora 42 KDE X11 with https://github.com/shiena/godot-camerafeed-demo, it works as expected, but I have some questions.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"474\" height=\"184\" alt=\"Screenshot_20250904_005235\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/204e6239-2492-44e0-be26-5922d3a79430\" />\r\n\r\nI can see with `--verbose` on startup it's adding the camera, removing it immediately then readding it:\r\n\r\n```\r\nCameraServer: Registered camera C922 Pro Stream Webcam (V4L2) with ID 1 and position 0 at index 0\r\nCameraServer: Removed camera C922 Pro Stream Webcam (V4L2) with ID 1 and position 0\r\nCameraServer: Registered camera C922 Pro Stream Webcam (V4L2) with ID 1 and position 0 at index 0\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlso, how can I check whether PipeWire was initialized correctly (or even compiled in correctly)? I didn't find this information in the verbose log. I did install `pipewire-devel` before compiling, but there's still `(V4L2)` in the suffix of the camera name, which makes me think it's not working.\r\n\r\nLastly, it seems changing the resolution and clicking **Reload** doesn't change the resolution (it goes back to the default 640×480). This happens even if I stop the stream beforehand (I see an error being printed if I change the resolution while the stream is active).\r\n\r\n\r\nEither way, this is still an improvement over `master`, where it constantly readded the same camera every second instead and made it unusable on this system:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"475\" height=\"578\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e83a89ad-728f-4a9e-98aa-bc3e02e85d10\" />","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109500#pullrequestreview-3182844396","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109500","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109500#pullrequestreview-3182844396"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109500"}},"submitted_at":"2025-09-03T23:09:18Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3258693379,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7CO7cD","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}"